  <entry>
    <title>Yiwu Trip Manifest</title>
    <link href="/2026/08/11/Yiwu-Trip-Manifest/"/>
    <url>/2026/08/11/Yiwu-Trip-Manifest/</url>
    
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Alita and I are driving to Yiwu — three days inside the world’s largest wholesale market, about 75,000 booths under one roof. We are treating it as a working trip rather than a sightseeing tour: see the supply chain first, then make her compute the numbers.</p><p>I put the whole plan on one page — the route from Shanghai, the budget, a day-by-day schedule, what to eat, and a field assignment for Alita that ends with her pitching a business idea to us on the drive home.</p><p><strong><a href="/yiwu/">→ Read the full trip manifest</a></strong></p><p>The page is password-protected — ask me for the password and it is yours. The checklists on it remember what you tick, so it works as a real planning document, not just something to read. Friends who want to make the same trip are welcome to use it.</p>]]></content>
    
    
    
